#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""oracle-gen — the oracle corpus's stores and queries, made from a fixed
seed so the corpus is the same on every run (ruling #91 R3).

    tools/oracle-gen     writes tests/oracle/stores/*.tsv and
                         tests/oracle/queries.jsonl

Five synthetic stores that look like real trees (a small home, a
developer's home, a monorepo, a system-and-home mix, a large org
checkout), 50 to 5,000 paths each. A store row is
`SCORE<TAB>AGE_SECONDS<TAB>COUNT<TAB>PATH`; ages sit well inside gump's
frecency buckets (minutes, hours, days, weeks) so a replay hours or
months later lands every entry in the same bucket. The queries are
derived from the stores' own paths: a last component whole, its prefix,
a fragment, an abbreviation, a typo (a letter dropped, two swapped, one
doubled), two and three terms in order and out of it, upper case, a
fragment with a slash, and words no path holds. tools/oracle-record asks
gump; tools/oracle-check asks lope.
"""
